instr:
`JsonParser.parse()` throws `not implemented` when editing JSON5

I hit this while using `@croct/json5-parser` to add a configuration setting without losing the document's comments and formatting.

```ts
import {JsonParser, JsonObjectNode} from '@croct/json5-parser';

const source = '{\n  // Connection settings\n  enabled: true,\n}';
const config = JsonParser.parse(source, JsonObjectNode);
config.set('retries', 4);
console.log(config.toString());
```

Parsing should produce an editable document, and writing it back should preserve the existing comments and layout while including the new setting. The API doc comments, where present, and `README.md`'s “Lexing”, “Parsing”, “Manipulation”, and “Formatting” sections describe the expected behavior for the lossless tokenizer, parser, and document editing support.

Instead, the parse call throws `Error: not implemented`. Unfinished stubs remain in `src/error.ts`, `src/lexer.ts`, `src/manipulator.ts`, `src/parser.ts`, and these files under `src/node/`: `arrayNode.ts`, `compositeNode.ts`, `identifierNode.ts`, `objectNode.ts`, `primitiveNode.ts`, `propertyNode.ts`, `structureNode.ts`, and `valueNode.ts`.

The fix should complete the unfinished parsing and editing support across those files and keep the package's own tests passing, preserving the existing public API names because callers import them.

The interface, the conventions and the sandbox limits for this change are written up in `FEATURE.md` at the repository root.
